# Alire crates (host build)

The repo is a **monorepo of Alire crates**, not one crate with many GPRs, and not many git remotes. **One Alire crate per Ada component**, each with its own `alire.toml` and a **single** `.gpr` whose name matches the crate (`lovelace_common.gpr` for crate `lovelace_common` in folder `common/`). **Every crate name starts with `lovelace`** (see utf8-and-naming). Alire’s unit is the crate: one dependency set, one crate type (library vs application), one runtime.

Do **not** list component GPRs in one `alire.toml` `project-files` array. Do **not** merge host libraries, the `lovelace` executable, and Augusta native into one crate.

## When to create a crate

Create an `alire.toml` / `.gpr` **only** when that component is required for the current task **or** the user explicitly asks. Do not scaffold the full crate graph, the workspace crate, test crates, or `shared/` ahead of time.

## Shared host switches

All **host** crates (full GNAT RTS) must `with` one abstract GPR and must **not** duplicate the switch list:

- Path: `shared/lovelace_host_switches.gpr` (a folder, **not** a crate)
- Create this file in the same change as the **first** host crate
- Contents: Ada 2022 and the mandatory host switches from the Ada standards rule (`-gnatwae`, `-gnaty…`, line length, `-gnato`, `-fstack-check`, `-gnatW8`)

Augusta **native** must **not** `with` that file (ZFP / freestanding; see Augusta rules). Nested **host** test crates `with` the same include.

## Root workspace crate

Thin aggregate at the **repository root** so `alr build` there builds everything that exists. Crate name **`lovelace_workspace`** (must not be `lovelace` — that name is the CLI crate in `lovelace/`). No Ada sources; only `[[depends-on]]` + path `[[pins]]` to crates that already exist. Create it only when asked, or when a root build is actually needed.

```toml
[[depends-on]]
lovelace_common = "*"

[[pins]]
lovelace_common = { path = "common" }
```

Pin paths are relative to that crate: `common` from the root, `../common` from `lovelace/`. Folder names are not crate names.

## Pins and layering

Local path pins, not separate repositories. Intended `depends-on` (do not add edges until both crates exist):

| Crate (folder) | Depends on (Lovelace siblings) |
|---|---|
| `lovelace_common` (`common/`) | — |
| `lovelace_lir` (`lir/`) | `lovelace_common` |
| `lovelace_compiler` (`compiler/`) | `lovelace_lir`, `lovelace_common` |
| `lovelace_tooling` (`tooling/`) | `lovelace_common` |
| `lovelace_format` (`format/`) | `lovelace_common`, `lovelace_tooling` |
| `lovelace_alexandria` (`alexandria/`) | `lovelace_common` |
| `lovelace_hypatia` (`hypatia/`) | `lovelace_tooling` (libgit2 only here) |
| `lovelace_jit` (`jit/`) | `lovelace_common` (Wasmtime C only here) |
| `lovelace` (`lovelace/`) | `lovelace_compiler`, `lovelace_jit`, `lovelace_tooling`, `lovelace_hypatia`, `lovelace_alexandria`, `lovelace_format` |
| `lovelace_augusta` (native, when created) | **none** of the host graph (JIT loads the `.so`/`.dll`/`.dylib` at run time) |

Do not `depends-on` a sibling just to share switches. Missing `depends-on` is how layering is enforced (`lovelace_compiler` must not see Hypatia/git; `lovelace_format` must not see Wasmtime).

## Tests and Augusta

AUnit is declared only on **nested** test crates (`common/tests` → crate `lovelace_common_tests`, …): own `alire.toml`, pin `{ path = ".." }`, `depends-on` the parent and AUnit. Nested test crate names also start with `lovelace`. Do not add AUnit to library or `lovelace` crates.

Augusta **`.love`** is not an Alire product. Only the native Ada backing is a crate (`Library_Kind use "dynamic"`).
